'' RUN: the classic file statements with non-ASCII names -- OPEN (output and input), FILEEXISTS,
'' FILELEN, FILEDATETIME, DIR, FILECOPY, NAME, KILL, MKDIR, CHDIR, CURDIR, RMDIR -- given as a
'' string, a ustring and a wstring, each checked against std/fs, which sees the name really on
'' disk; a file std/fs made, found by the classic statements; and on Windows an ANSI byte name
'' (the code-page fallback). A deliberate divergence from fbc, whose runtime reads the bytes as
'' the ANSI code page: 'ñ' lands as 'Ã±' and a wstring '日本' fails. Needs the runtime of this
'' commit, so it passes only once the toolchain is repackaged (it links the packaged libfb.a).
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/unicode-paths.tiko -o tests/codegen/unicodepaths.exe
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/codegen/unicodepaths.exe
'' RUN: tests/codegen/unicodepaths.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: ok
